{
  "slug": "public-speaking-and-presentations",
  "concept": "Public Speaking and Presentations",
  "generated": "2026-09-08",
  "summary": "Answer four questions before touching a slide tool:",
  "facets": [
    {
      "title": "Audience Analysis Before You Open PowerPoint",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Answer four questions before touching a slide tool:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#audience-analysis-before-you-open-powerpoint",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Who is in the room? Job function, seniority, and domain expertise.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#audience-analysis-before-you-open-powerpoint",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "What do they already believe? Start from their current position.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#audience-analysis-before-you-open-powerpoint",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "What one action do you want them to take? Name the action.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#audience-analysis-before-you-open-powerpoint",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "What is the one thing they must remember? Write that sentence before slide 1.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#audience-analysis-before-you-open-powerpoint",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Slide-Doc vs Presentation Slides",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Presentation slides (Reynolds / \"Presentation Zen\" model) exist to support a live speaker. The speaker carries the argument; the slide carries visual reinforcement. One idea per slide. Minimal text. Large images or diagrams.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#slide-doc-vs-presentation-slides",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Slide-docs (Tufte-influenced) are standalone documents formatted as slide-shaped pages. They contain complete sentences, dense supporting data, footnotes. They can be emailed and read without a presenter.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#slide-doc-vs-presentation-slides",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "The core failure mode: the slidument - bullet-heavy slides that are too dense to look good on screen and too sparse to be useful to a reader.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#slide-doc-vs-presentation-slides",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Kawasaki 10/20/30 Rule",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "10 slides - humans can't absorb more than ten concepts in a single sitting",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#kawasaki-102030-rule",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "20 minutes - even if you have a full hour, present in 20 minutes",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#kawasaki-102030-rule",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "30-point minimum font - if you cannot fit your message in 30pt type, you have too many words",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#kawasaki-102030-rule",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Nancy Duarte's Resonate Framework",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The central insight: every great speech moves back and forth between \"what is\" and \"what could be.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#nancy-duartes-resonate-framework",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "The contrast pattern:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#nancy-duartes-resonate-framework",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Establish the current reality (what is)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#nancy-duartes-resonate-framework",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Describe the future possibility (what could be)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#nancy-duartes-resonate-framework",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Repeat this oscillation; each cycle raises the stakes",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#nancy-duartes-resonate-framework",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "End with the \"new bliss\" - the world after the audience acts",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#nancy-duartes-resonate-framework",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "The STAR moment (Something They'll Always Remember): one designed moment of high contrast, surprise, or visceral demonstration.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#nancy-duartes-resonate-framework",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Three-Act Talk Structure",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Act 1 - Setup (10–15% of total time): Establish stakes; define the problem; signal what the audience will be able to do differently by the end.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#three-act-talk-structure",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Act 2 - Exploration (70–75%): Develop the argument. Front-load complex material; place a re-energizing moment two-thirds of the way through.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#three-act-talk-structure",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Act 3 - Resolution (10–15%): Do not introduce new material. Synthesize, do not summarize.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#three-act-talk-structure",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The Headline-Deck Approach (McKinsey / BCG)",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Every slide title is a complete, standalone sentence stating the takeaway, not a topic label.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#the-headline-deck-approach-mckinsey-bcg",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Bad title: \"Market Analysis\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#the-headline-deck-approach-mckinsey-bcg",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Good title: \"The North American market is growing 12% YoY and outpacing EMEA in every segment.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#the-headline-deck-approach-mckinsey-bcg",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "A reader who reads only slide titles should follow the full argument.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#the-headline-deck-approach-mckinsey-bcg",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Talk Openings — Five Patterns",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Startling fact or statistic: drop a number the audience does not expect",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#talk-openings-five-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Story: open with a specific scene - one person, one moment, sensory detail",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#talk-openings-five-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Contrarian claim: state something the audience believes that you are about to challenge",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#talk-openings-five-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Direct question: ask a question the audience cannot immediately answer",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#talk-openings-five-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Scene-setting: describe the world as it will look after your idea is adopted",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#talk-openings-five-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Do not open with: your name and title, an apology, \"great to be here,\" agenda slides.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#talk-openings-five-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Talk Closings — Five Patterns",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Callback to opening: return to the story or question you opened with",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#talk-closings-five-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Call to action: one specific, concrete thing the audience can do in the next 48 hours",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#talk-closings-five-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Single image or quote: full-bleed slide with one sentence",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#talk-closings-five-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Summary triple: three short phrases that encapsulate the talk's three main points",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#talk-closings-five-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "The future vision: describe the world three years from now if the audience acts",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#talk-closings-five-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Q&A Handling",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The bridging technique: acknowledge the question, then bridge to your main message.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#qa-handling",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "\"I don't know\" as a complete answer: say it cleanly, then add \"I'll find out and get back to you by [date].\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#qa-handling",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Hostile questions: do not match the energy. Lower your voice slightly. Answer the question beneath the question.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#qa-handling",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Rehearsal Discipline",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Minimum effective rehearsal for a 30-minute talk:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#rehearsal-discipline",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Three times out loud, alone - full volume, full sentences, full transitions",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#rehearsal-discipline",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Once to a real human - their confusion is signal",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#rehearsal-discipline",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Video review of yourself - watch on mute first (body language), then with sound (pace and filler)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#rehearsal-discipline",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Pacing target: 125–150 words per minute. Time your talk at 90% of the slot.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#rehearsal-discipline",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Virtual vs In-Person Calibration",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Virtual: look at the camera lens, not at faces on screen. Place the camera at eye level.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#virtual-vs-in-person-calibration",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Audio quality (virtual): audio quality matters more than video quality. A USB condenser microphone, a quiet room, and a soft surface behind you.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#virtual-vs-in-person-calibration",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Energy calibration (virtual): increase vocal variety noticeably above what feels natural in a room - the camera flattens affect.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#virtual-vs-in-person-calibration",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Anti-Patterns to Eliminate",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Reading slides verbatim.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#anti-patterns-to-eliminate",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Walls of bullets. Each bullet resets the audience's attention to near-zero.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#anti-patterns-to-eliminate",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "\"As you can see here...\" - If it is visible, do not narrate its existence.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#anti-patterns-to-eliminate",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Apologizing for slides.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#anti-patterns-to-eliminate",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Running long. Going over time disrespects every person in the room.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#anti-patterns-to-eliminate",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "The vague closing. \"So, in conclusion, we looked at X, Y, and Z...\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/public-speaking-and-presentations/#anti-patterns-to-eliminate",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
